## Next native RF evidence boundary (source audit, 2026-11-10)

The normal native PCI owner already produces a same-epoch `NvmBoardSelection`
with valid AR9565 gain profiles and completes PMU/XTAL capacitor writes.
`Ar9565RadioSequence` can consume that board and run the ordered receive-only
INI, PHY, modal, RF-bus, PLL, synthesizer, OFDM, RX calibration and ANI stages,
but `SimpleATH` does **not** invoke it yet because the following physical
inputs have no authorized producer:

- **Reference crystal identity:** Linux v6.12 `ar9003_phy.c`
  (`ar9003_hw_set_channel`) chooses distinct fractional synth divisors for
  `ah->is_clk_25mhz` (75 for 25 MHz, 120 for 40 MHz) on AR9565. Its reset,
  PLL and radio table paths also branch on that field. The physical PCI ID
  and EEPROM capacitor setting do not, by themselves, prove 25 vs 40 MHz.
  Preserve `RfReferenceClock` as unverified until a real same-board firmware,
  ACPI/platform or other physical clock authority establishes it; do not
  default to either branch or reuse an earlier reset epoch.
- **Antenna/BT coexistence ownership:** `ar9003_phy.c` includes explicit
  AR9565 antenna-diversity programming; `ar9003_mci.c` has separate AR9565
  coexistence branches. The physical USB firmware-loader personality does
  not prove that BT is absent, permanently quiesced, or has negotiated an
  antenna/MCI lease. Native post-bootstrap USB/HCI status and independent
  physical antenna arbitration are still needed before setting the
  `coexistenceConfigurationVerified` and antenna proof bits.
- **Receive channel permission:** an EEPROM-supported frequency and a user
  scan request are not the same as independent platform-regulatory approval.
  Implement one same-epoch 2.4 GHz receive-channel lease with a real country
  policy, then run the sequence and read back its actual completion before
  setting `radioOperational_`, `channelAuthorized_` or
  `verifiedReceiveChannel_`. Retain stricter TX country/CTL/TPC proof before
  *any* data, management or automatic response is enabled.

Commits `8edfbe0` and `e7bbcf9` now connect a correctly gated initial EDMA
